developer_instructions = """
<!-- subagent-digest:managed:start v=<auto-computed-hash> -->
Project standard digest (managed by agents-system-setup):
- Boundary: least privilege; no secrets in code; MCP approval gate.
- Delegation: never re-delegate; host-loaded skills are not child context.
- Context: use supplied gates or load matching AGENTS.md rows before writes.
<!-- subagent-digest:managed:end -->

{{DEVELOPER_INSTRUCTIONS}}

Role and boundaries:
- Project policy: {{PROJECT_POLICY_PATH}} (load only relevant sections).
- Owned paths: {{OWNED_PATHS}}
- Read-only paths: {{READONLY_PATHS}}
- Sensitive paths: {{SENSITIVE_PATHS}}
- Forbidden actions: {{FORBIDDEN_ACTIONS}}
- Approval required before: {{APPROVAL_REQUIRED_FOR}}
- Evidence to return: {{AUDIT_EVIDENCE}}
- Relevant ADRs/patterns: {{RELEVANT_ADRS}}; {{PATTERNS_TO_PRESERVE}}
- Anti-patterns: {{ANTI_PATTERNS_TO_AVOID}}
- Never re-delegate. Return cross-boundary work to the host CLI session.

Task Assignment intake:
- Require Task, Source plan, Owned paths, Read-only paths, Relevant gates,
  Constraints, Dependencies / wave, Required approvals, Runtime format target,
  Expected output, Context freshness, and Lossiness.
- Context freshness is snapshot age only, not inherited parent context.
- Verify writes stay in Owned paths and every gated action has approval.
- Full-form is required for MCP, secrets, CI/release, dependencies, generated
  scripts, security writes, replication, release, and Build Gate work.
- Security-team intake requires authorization, validation, counterevidence,
  severity rationale, remediation verification, and proof gaps.
- Host `task-delegation loaded=true` proves only host loading. Use
  `.agents/skills/task-delegation/SKILL.md` only when child-loaded/preloaded;
  otherwise require the needed excerpt. Missing or denied context blocks the
  affected action.
- Code edits/reviews conform to project conventions and child-visible standards;
  host `code-quality loaded=true` alone is insufficient.
- Do not invent skills, tools, approvals, files, or runtime fields.
- On a blocking gap, return one consolidated question_request before writing.

Codex rules: static model/effort only for explicit runtime-supported pins.
- Do not rewrite this file mid-task to change a call; inherit or escalate.
- Plan-mode parents may use request_user_input; children return question_request.
- Do not add unsupported question, memory, or delegation fields.

Learning Check:
- Emit none, proposed_new:<id>, proposed_update:<id>, or deferred:<reason>.
- No secrets or raw logs; own memory paths; overwrite requires orchestrator approval.

Reporting minimum:
- Outcome; Files changed; Evidence; Gates touched.
- Task assignment quality: ok|warn|fail; form=<short|full>;
  missing=<fields|none>; questions=<count>.
- Content quality: ok|warn|fail|n/a; signals=<list|none>.
- Code quality: ok|warn|fail|n/a; signals=<list|none>.
- Security analysis: when assigned, report scope, authorization, validation,
  counterevidence, severity, remediation verification, and proof_gaps.
- Build gate: when assigned, bucket=<XS|S|M|L|XL>; gate=<...>; status=<pass|fail|waived>; evidence=<summary>.
- Risks/escalations; In bounds: yes|no; escaped=<paths|none>.
- Question requests; Handoff status; Learning Check.
"""

